From c0bf2d0f0b3be68c44e8d948c575bb6cae936c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:15:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] placement: home-relative .hermes span ends at the
 next cd (linear); cd into ~/.hermes pins

PR #2463 review 5895947424 nits, applied to main's HERMES_STATE_PATH (907d09c9f6b):

1. Over-match: the `_CD_HOME + [\s\S]*?` span ran to the end of the card, so
   `cd ~ && git clone x repo && cd repo && write .hermes/plans/p.md` pinned as
   state-path and the pool verdict read it as ~/.hermes/plans/p.md. The span is
   now tempered: it stops at the next `cd`/`pushd`/`popd` (lowercase only, so
   prose "CI/CD" does not end it; a `cd .hermes` itself does not end it).
2. Performance: with no match that span made the search quadratic in
   (cd count) x (text length). Each start now reads only to the next directory
   change: 334 KB / 5000 `cd ~` lines 18.3 s -> 0.05 s.
3. Fail-open: `cd ~/.hermes && cat .env` (any home spelling, quoted, trailing
   slash, `pushd`, or `cd .hermes` after a cd home) named no state marker. A
   cd/pushd into the state directory now pins. A bare `~/.hermes` elsewhere
   still does not: 9328cbc2d9b made "the hermes-agent tree under ~/.hermes"
   worker-first (test_ordinary_repo_work_enrolls_worker_first goes RED if it
   pins). `_strip_read_paths` already keeps text with such a cd (`_CHDIR`), so a
   declared hub:read never clears it; comment + rows say so.

Also closes the residual gaps #2463's rows found on main: `./.hermes/` after a
cd home, and the pool verdict now reads every home-relative hit as
`~/.hermes/<p>`, so a worker's own artifact named after `cd ~` keeps the card
(class a-artifact) instead of going to hub-write.

Rebased onto 49f0ccd4a5e (PR #2460 nits: pushd home, commented/redirected cd,
lowercase cd, span stopping at the next cd HOME): its `_CD_HOME`, `_REL_STATE`
and fallback naming are kept; this commit widens the span stop to ANY
cd/pushd/popd, which is what fixes nit 1 (49f0ccd4a5e kept the over-match).

Tests: #2463's rows (test_kanban_placement_home_spellings.py new, hunks in
test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py / test_kanban_pool_queue.py) plus new rows for the
three nits, incl. a timing bound on a 334 KB no-match body.
RED on base: 34 failed / 272 passed across the 4 placement-path files (timing
row: 16.7 s against a 1 s bound). GREEN: 96 files importing kanban_placement,
2652 passed, 0 failed.
